---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={"Bang My Twister — Historic Max for Live Device and Current Setup — Auspicious Music"}
  description={"A Max for Live device for the MIDI Fighter Twister published here in 2014, documented with its verified external source and a current equivalent."}
  canonicalPath={"/legacy/bang-my-twister/"}
  lang={"en"}
  noindex={false}
  loadStringField={false}
>
<Fragment slot="head">
<style is:global>
@layer components {
  .pg-head { padding-block: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem) clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem); }
  .pg-head h1 { max-width: 17ch; margin-top: 1.25rem; }
  .pg-head .lede { margin-top: 1.5rem; max-width: 58ch; }
  .pg-head--dark { background: var(--dark); color: var(--dark-text); padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem); }
  .pg-head--dark .crumbs { color: var(--dark-muted); }
  .pg-head--dark .crumbs a:hover { color: var(--dark-text); }
  .pg-head--dark .lede { color: var(--dark-muted); }

  .prose { max-width: var(--measure); }
  .prose > * + * { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .prose h2 { font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 1.2rem + 1.2vw, 2rem); letter-spacing: -0.016em; margin-top: clamp(2.75rem, 5vw, 3.75rem); }
  .prose h3 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin-top: 2rem; letter-spacing: -0.012em; }
  .prose p { color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .prose a:not(.link):not(.btn) { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }

  .rule-list li {
    padding-block: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.75rem minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft); line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .rule-list li:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .rule-list li::before {
    content: ""; inline-size: 7px; block-size: 7px; border-radius: 50%;
    background: transparent; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px var(--line-strong); margin-top: 0.62rem;
  }
  .rule-list strong { color: var(--ink); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }

  .callout { border-left: 2px solid var(--ink); padding: 0.25rem 0 0.25rem 1.5rem; }
  .callout strong { display: block; margin-bottom: 0.375rem; }
  .callout p { color: var(--ink); }

  .facts { display: grid; gap: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--dark-line); margin-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem); }
  .facts > div {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(8rem, 12rem) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.5rem 1.5rem; padding-block: 0.875rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--dark-line-soft);
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--t-meta);
    letter-spacing: var(--tr-meta); line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .facts dt { color: var(--dark-muted); }
  .facts dd { color: var(--dark-text); }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { .facts > div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.1875rem; } }

  .timeline { position: relative; padding-left: 2rem; }
  .timeline::before { content: ""; position: absolute; left: 3px; top: 1.2rem; bottom: 1.2rem; width: 1px; background: var(--line-strong); }
  .timeline li { position: relative; padding-block: 1.125rem; }
  .timeline li + li { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .timeline li::before {
    content: ""; position: absolute; left: -2rem; top: 1.7rem;
    inline-size: 7px; block-size: 7px; border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--canvas); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px var(--line-strong);
  }
  .timeline li:last-child::before { background: var(--ember-bright); box-shadow: none; }
  .timeline time { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--t-meta); letter-spacing: var(--tr-meta); color: var(--muted); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.375rem; }
  .timeline h3 { font-size: 1.125rem; letter-spacing: -0.011em; margin: 0 0 0.375rem; }
  .timeline p { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 58ch; }

  .listing li { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .listing li:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .listing a {
    display: grid; gap: 0.375rem 2.5rem; padding-block: 1.375rem;
    text-decoration: none; align-items: baseline;
    transition: background-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease);
  }
  .listing a:hover { background: var(--surface); }
  .listing h3 { font-size: 1.25rem; letter-spacing: -0.014em; }
  .listing p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.55; max-width: 58ch; }
  .listing__tail { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--t-meta); letter-spacing: var(--tr-meta); color: var(--muted); }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .listing a { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 16rem) minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 9rem); align-items: start; }
    .listing__tail { text-align: right; padding-top: 0.3rem; }
  }

  .glossary > div { padding-block: 1.125rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .glossary > div:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .glossary dt { font-weight: 550; font-size: 1.0625rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .glossary dd { color: var(--muted); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.6; margin-top: 0.25rem; max-width: 60ch; }

  .sources { margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem); padding-top: 2rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .sources h2 { font-size: var(--t-h3); margin: 0 0 1.25rem; }
  .sources ol { display: grid; gap: 0.875rem; counter-reset: src; }
  .sources li { counter-increment: src; padding-left: 2rem; position: relative; font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--muted); }
  .sources li::before { content: counter(src); position: absolute; left: 0; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--t-meta); }
  .sources a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
}
</style>
</Fragment>

<main id="content">

  <section class="pg-head pg-head--dark" data-od-id="page-head">
    <div class="shell">
      <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <ol>
          <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
          <li><a href="/download/">Archive</a></li>
          <li>Bang My Twister</li>
        </ol>
      </nav>
      <p class="flag" style="margin-top:1.5rem">Historical resource<br>Independent relaunch under new ownership</p>
      <h1>Bang My Twister</h1>
      <p class="lede">A Max for Live device for switching banks on the DJ TechTools MIDI Fighter Twister, published on this domain in 2014 by the former operator. The original mapping is still maintained by DJ TechTools, so this page points there rather than rehosting a copy.</p>
      
      <dl class="facts">
        <div><dt>Historical period</dt><dd>2014</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Former operator</dt><dd>Previous owner of this domain</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Original format</dt><dd>Max for Live device · controller mapping</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Rights status</dt><dd>Mapping remains with DJ TechTools</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Verified externally</dt><dd>Yes — mapping still published</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Page reviewed</dt><dd>August 2026</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p style="margin-top:2rem"><a class="btn btn--quiet" href="https://maps.djtechtools.com/mappings/2929" rel="noopener">Open the mapping at DJ TechTools</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>


  <section class="band" data-od-id="legacy-body">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2 style="margin-top:0">What the original project was</h2>
        <p>
          The MIDI Fighter Twister has sixteen encoders. A Live set almost always has more
          than sixteen parameters worth reaching, which is the problem bank switching
          exists to solve: each encoder addresses a different parameter depending on which
          page is active.
        </p>
        <p>
          Bang My Twister was a small Max for Live device that handled that switching from
          inside the Live set rather than from the controller's own configuration utility.
          It was published here alongside a visualiser project and circulated through the
          controller community of the period.
        </p>

        <h2>Why external sources still point here</h2>
        <p>
          The device was listed in the DJ TechTools mapping archive, which is still online
          and still maintained. That is a live, verifiable reference rather than an
          archived one — the reason this address returns a page instead of a redirect, and
          the reason the download status here reads as external rather than unavailable.
        </p>

        <h2>Current status</h2>
        <p>
          The mapping is available from DJ TechTools, who publish and maintain it. This
          publication does not host a copy: a rehosted mapping goes stale the moment the
          original is updated, and the version here would quietly become the wrong one.
        </p>
        <div class="callout">
          <p>
            <strong>Compatibility has not been re-tested by us.</strong>
            The device dates from 2014 and Live has had several major versions since. A
            current compatibility test is planned; until it has been run, this page does
            not claim the device still works.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h2>Rights and attribution</h2>
        <p>
          The device was created and published by the former operator of this domain; the
          controller and its mapping archive belong to DJ TechTools. Auspicious Music is
          an independent publication under new ownership since 2026 and claims no part of
          either. Nothing here should be read as a continuation of, or endorsement by,
          the former operator.
        </p>

        <h2>How the same thing is done now</h2>
        <p>
          Bank switching no longer needs a bespoke device in most cases. The controller's
          own configuration utility handles multiple banks natively, and Live's mapping
          has improved considerably since 2014. Where a set genuinely needs switching
          driven from inside Live, a small Max device remains the way to do it — the
          approach is covered in the <a href="/ableton/">Ableton hub</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Change log</h2>
        <ul class="timeline" data-reveal-group>
          <li data-reveal><time datetime="2014">2014</time><p>Device announced and published by the former operator, and listed in the DJ TechTools mapping archive.</p></li>
          <li data-reveal><time datetime="2017">2017</time><p>Last archived capture of the original page. The site stops being maintained shortly afterwards.</p></li>
          <li data-reveal><time datetime="2026-02">February 2026</time><p>Domain acquired by the current publisher. External reference confirmed still live.</p></li>
          <li data-reveal><time datetime="2026-08">August 2026</time><p>This page published. Download status recorded as external; compatibility test outstanding.</p></li>
        </ul>

        <div class="sources">
          <h2>Sources and original references</h2>
          <ol>
            <li><a href="https://maps.djtechtools.com/mappings/2929" rel="noopener">DJ TechTools mapping archive</a> — the original mapping, still published and maintained.</li>
            <li>Internet Archive Wayback Machine — captures of this domain, 2014 to 2017.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section data-od-id="relaunch-notice">
    <div class="shell relaunch">
      <p>Auspicious Music was relaunched under new ownership in 2026. Historical
         references are preserved for context.</p>
      <a class="link" href="/about/history-and-relaunch/">Read the history and relaunch note
        <svg viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>
</BaseLayout>